lexSans-Regular-2d\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-15\" transform=\"translate(59.59375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-12\" transform=\"translate(95.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-13\" transform=\"translate(151.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-12\" transform=\"translate(209.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-16\" transform=\"translate(265.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-6\" transform=\"translate(314.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-5\" transform=\"translate(369.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e9\" transform=\"translate(427.40625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-70\" transform=\"translate(451 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-e\" transform=\"translate(484.5 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-3e9\" transform=\"translate(537.203125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-19\" transform=\"translate(560.796875 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-c\" transform=\"translate(610 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-16\" transform=\"translate(635 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-c\" transform=\"translate(683.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-17\" transform=\"translate(708.703125 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-12\" transform=\"translate(743.390625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-15\" transform=\"translate(799.390625 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-16\" transform=\"translate(836.09375 0)\"/><use xlink:href=\"#IBMPlexSans-Regular-71\" transform=\"translate(884.796875 0)\"/></g></g></g></g></g><defs><clipPath id=\"p851f1e2de3\"><rect x=\"46.1\" y=\"28\" width=\"345.96\" height=\"133.056\"/></clipPath></defs></svg>\n","title":"Exhibit 1 · Visitors by time slot (k)","note":null},"answer":"<p>Today: 900k × ($18 − $3) = <b>$13.50M</b>.</p> <p>After: peak 540k → 497k at $21 margin; off-peak 360k → 414k at $11 margin.</p> <p>Contribution: <b>$14.99M</b> (+$1.49M, 11%). Visitors: <b>911k</b> (+11k).</p> <p><b>So-what:</b> more income, slightly more visitors, and 43k fewer people in the weekend queues. It meets the city's conditions.</p>"},{"q":"Critics say $24 shuts out families. How would you protect access?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li>Keep <b>free first Sundays</b> for residents, with timed booking so they don't queue</li> <li><b>Under-18s free</b> and student tickets at the off-peak price at any time</li> <li>A <b>resident annual pass</b> (e.g. $30) valid at any time</li> <li>Publish the income raised and the restorations it pays for</li></ul>"},{"q":"What would make you less confident in the forecast?","exhibit":null,"answer":"<ul><li>Off-peak growth may come mainly from people switching days, not new visitors: income still rises, but total visits might not</li> <li>Tour groups may book elsewhere if they lose flexibility</li><li>Bad weather and events shift demand between slots</li></ul> <p>Test it for a summer season before making it permanent.</p>"}],"reco":"Introduce peak and off-peak pricing: $24 at weekends and holidays, $14 on weekday mornings, in timed slots. On the research estimates, contribution rises from $13.5M to $15.0M, total visitors rise to about 911k and weekend crowding falls. Protect access with free first Sundays, free entry for under-18s and a low-cost resident pass. Risk: off-peak growth may be smaller if it's mostly people switching days. Next step: pilot for one summer season and measure visits by slot.","great":["Respects the public mission as a constraint","Calculates both income and visitor numbers","Uses price to spread demand, not just raise income","Builds in protections for access"],"id":37,"slug":"cobalt-museums"}